---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/global.css";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Restaurant",
  name: "Chateau Marmont",
  servesCuisine: ["American"],
  priceRange: "$$$",
  telephone: "+1-323-656-1010",
  url: "https://www.chateaumarmont.com",
  address: {
    "@type": "PostalAddress",
    streetAddress: "8221 Sunset Blvd",
    addressLocality: "West Hollywood",
    addressRegion: "CA",
    postalCode: "90046",
    addressCountry: "US",
  },
  description:
    "Historic hotel restaurant on the Sunset Strip in West Hollywood, led by executive chef Dean Yasharian.",
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Chateau Marmont Menu Guide (2026) — Prices, What to Order | Hotel Menu Guide"
  description="An independent guide to the Chateau Marmont restaurant in West Hollywood: chef Dean Yasharian's American menu with dated reported prices, hours, reservations, and visiting tips. Verify prices before visiting."
  path="/chateau-marmont-menu/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  ogImage="/images/chateau-marmont-dining.webp"
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
    <img
      src="/images/chateau-marmont-dining.webp"
      alt="Illustration of the Chateau Marmont's garden terrace restaurant at dusk"
      class="w-full h-64 sm:h-96 object-cover rounded-2xl mt-8"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />

    <p class="mt-8 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-gold-dark">
      Menu Guide · West Hollywood
    </p>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mt-2 leading-tight">
      Chateau Marmont — Menu Guide
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      The dining room at the Chateau Marmont sits inside one of the most mythologized buildings in
      Los Angeles: a 1929 apartment house modeled on a Loire Valley royal residence, converted to a
      hotel during the Depression and famous ever since as a hideaway for Greta Garbo, Marilyn Monroe,
      Clark Gable, Elizabeth Taylor, Jim Morrison, and Mick Jagger. Columbia Pictures founder Harry
      Cohn once said, "If you must get in trouble, do it at the Chateau Marmont." The restaurant
      itself is far calmer than the legend — American comfort food in a casual-elegant room (and on
      the famous garden terrace), led by executive chef Dean Yasharian. Below is our independent
      walkthrough of the menu, hours, and what we'd order. Everything is written in our own words;
      prices are reported figures, not a copy of the restaurant's menu — and the itemized prices
      below come from a published 2022 menu, so treat them as dated.
    </p>

    <!-- At a glance -->
    <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-6 sm:p-8">
      <h2 class="!mt-0 font-display text-xl font-bold">At a glance</h2>
      <dl class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 text-sm">
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Location</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">8221 Sunset Blvd, West Hollywood, CA 90046 (inside Chateau Marmont)</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Chef</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Executive Chef Dean Yasharian</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Cuisine</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">American (dining style: casual elegant)</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Price level</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">No current published prices; the 2022 menu ran roughly $15–$46 per dish — verify before visiting</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Reservations</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Via Resy through the official site; not bookable on OpenTable — the hotel asks guests to call ahead</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Phone</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">+1 (323) 656-1010</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-guide">
      <h2>Hours (reported)</h2>
      <p>
        The reported schedule, from the restaurant's OpenTable listing, is: breakfast Monday–Friday
        6:30–11:00 AM and Saturday–Sunday 6:30 AM–12:00 PM; lunch Monday–Friday 11:00 AM–5:00 PM and
        Saturday–Sunday 12:00–5:00 PM; dinner daily 5:00 PM–12:00 midnight. These hours are undated in
        the source, so confirm with the restaurant before planning around them.
      </p>

      <h2>Starters &amp; small plates</h2>
      <p>
        The opening section reads like classic hotel-dining comfort: an iceberg wedge with bacon,
        walnuts and blue cheese dressing; a Caesar; beef carpaccio; crispy calamari; a charcuterie
        and cheese board with pickles and celeriac rémoulade; and a falafel plate. Reported prices
        from the published <strong>2022 menu (dated)</strong> run roughly <strong>$15–$26</strong>.
      </p>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line my-6 not-prose">
        <table class="w-full text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-parchment text-left">
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Dish</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-right">Reported price (2022, dated)</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-line bg-white">
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Spaghetti Bolognese</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$15</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Caesar Salad</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$16</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Crispy Calamari</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$16</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Bucatini &amp; Clams</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$16</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Iceberg Wedge</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$17</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Mushroom Ravioli</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$17</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Beef Carpaccio</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$21</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Grilled Octopus</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$22</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Charcuterie &amp; Cheese</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$26</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Falafel</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$26</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        Our take: the grilled octopus — paired with watermelon, arugula and lemon vinaigrette on the
        2022 menu — is the most interesting plate here, and the charcuterie board is the easy
        crowd-pleaser if the table wants to graze.
      </p>

      <h2>Mains</h2>
      <p>
        The main courses stay in comfort territory: pastas, a burger, a Sunday fried chicken, and a
        handful of fish and meat plates. Reported <strong>2022 (dated)</strong> prices run roughly
        <strong>$20–$46</strong>.
      </p>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line my-6 not-prose">
        <table class="w-full text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-parchment text-left">
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Dish</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-right">Reported price (2022, dated)</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-line bg-white">
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Black Truffle Risotto</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$20</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Chateau Burger</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$23</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Buttermilk Fried Chicken (Sundays)</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$29</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Roasted Chicken</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$32</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">King Salmon</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$33</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Bouillabaisse</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$35</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">White Sea Bass</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$35</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Lamb</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$42</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Steak Frites</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$46</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        The steak frites — a dry-aged New York strip with fries and béarnaise — sat at the top of
        the 2022 menu. The bouillabaisse brings saffron fish broth with tiger prawns, mussels and
        rouille, and the Sunday-only buttermilk fried chicken comes with kale, mashed potatoes and
        gravy, a biscuit and spiced honey. Dessert on the 2022 menu was a tapioca pudding with
        spiced pineapple, lime financier and coconut sorbet, reported at <strong>$12 (dated)</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2>Breakfast</h2>
      <p>
        Reported breakfast prices come from an <strong>undated</strong> third-party listing, so treat
        them as rough figures only: eggs Benedict, huevos rancheros, breakfast burrito and bagel
        &amp; lox around <strong>$22</strong>; croque madame <strong>$20</strong>; a three-egg omelette
        <strong>$21</strong>; buttermilk pancakes <strong>$17</strong>; Chateau granola <strong>$15</strong>;
        and coffee <strong>$6–$10</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2>What we'd order</h2>
      <p>If we had one meal here, this is how we'd play it:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>To start:</strong> the grilled octopus — the most distinctive plate on the reported menu.</li>
        <li><strong>The main event:</strong> steak frites on a regular night; the Sunday buttermilk fried chicken if you're lucky enough to be there on a Sunday.</li>
        <li><strong>The value move:</strong> the Chateau burger — the lowest-priced main on the 2022 menu, and a proper hotel burger with cheddar, house pickle and fries.</li>
        <li><strong>To finish:</strong> the tapioca pudding — the one dessert the old menu offered, and it sounds like the kind of retro dish that suits this room.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Planning your visit</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Book through Resy</strong> via the official site — the restaurant isn't on OpenTable, and the hotel asks guests to call ahead for restaurant or bar reservations.</li>
        <li><strong>Confirm hours and prices before you go.</strong> The only itemized menu we found was last updated in February 2022, and the hours come from an undated listing — a quick call to +1 (323) 656-1010 clears both up.</li>
        <li><strong>Dress code</strong> is listed as smart casual, with valet parking available.</li>
        <li><strong>Celebrity-discretion culture applies</strong> — this is a room where famous people go to be left alone, so keep the camera down in the dining room.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Price disclaimer -->
    <div class="mt-10 rounded-xl border border-gold/40 bg-gold/10 p-5 text-sm text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      <p class="font-semibold text-ink mb-1">About these prices</p>
      <p>
        Prices above are reported figures, <strong>not current prices</strong>. The itemized menu
        prices come from a menu published in <strong>February 2022 (dated)</strong> and are almost
        certainly higher today; the breakfast figures come from an undated third-party listing. We
        could not find a current published menu. Always verify current prices — and hours — with the
        restaurant before visiting.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-ink-soft">
      <a href="/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">← Back to all guides</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
